Description: gate examples shebang sed on nodoc so the rule no-ops cleanly
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-21
Bug-Athena: libxml-parser-perl's override_dh_installexamples runs
 `sed -i -e'1s|/usr/local/bin/perl|/usr/bin/perl|' $(EG)/canonical
 $(EG)/xmlcomments $(EG)/xmlstats $(EG)/xmlfilter` to rewrite the
 example scripts' shebang line.
 .
 Under DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc, dh_installexamples is a no-op, so
 $(EG) (= debian/libxml-parser-perl/usr/share/doc/libxml-parser-perl/
 examples) is never created.  sed then fails with
   sed: can't read .../examples/canonical: No such file or directory
 and the build dies at debian/rules:33.
 .
 Fix: wrap the sed in `ifeq (,$(findstring nodoc,$(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)))`
 so the rule no-ops cleanly when nodoc is active.  Behaviour without
 nodoc is unchanged — the sed still rewrites the example shebangs.
 .
 TEMPORARY: nodoc is a workaround for missing doc-build tooling in
 the build pool, not a permanent policy.  DELETE THIS PATCH when
 CONF-08 lands and nodoc is dropped from [Source] BuildOptions /
 BuildProfiles in config/build.conf.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -30,7 +30,9 @@

 override_dh_installexamples:
 	dh_installexamples
+ifeq (,$(findstring nodoc,$(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)))
 	sed -i -e'1s|/usr/local/bin/perl|/usr/bin/perl|' $(EG)/canonical $(EG)/xmlcomments $(EG)/xmlstats $(EG)/xmlfilter
+endif

 # install Encodings/README and Encodings/*.msg as documentation
 override_dh_install:
